time required: 20 minutes
ingredient_count: 10
---

Heat the @olive oil{2%tsp} in a #skillet{} over medium-high heat. Add the @onion{1/2}(diced) and @chipotle pepper in adobo{1%canned}(minced). Cook for ~{4-5%minutes} until the onion begins to soften. Add the @garlic{2%cloves}(minced) and @oregano{1/2%tsp}. Cook for about ~{1%minute} until fragrant.

Add the @canned black beans{28%oz}(drained and rinsed), @tomato paste{1%tbsp}, and @water{2%tbsp}. Stir to combine and cook for about ~{5%minutes} until tomato paste has fully dissolved and the beans are warmed through.

Taste and season with @salt{} and @pepper{} as needed. Serve in warm @corn tortillas{8} with fresh @cilantro{1/4%cup}(chopped).

> Topping ideas: avocado, chopped tomatoes, finely sliced cabbage, queso fresco, jalapenos, radishes, fresh limes, sour cream, salsa, etc.